  "body": "**Stacked on #1020** (#818, `issue/818-swing-any-horizontal`): this branch starts from #1020's head, so until #1020 merges the diff below also shows its commit. Retarget/merge order per AGENTS.md \"Overlapping issues stack\". Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\nWorks #821 as corrected by its 2026-11-11 comment: the microARC subplate does **not** turn with A - it is a base plate that mounts the rotary on a fixture plate (two pin bores) or on the T-slots. The safety core: the index-swing check (#804/#810/#818) assumed the machine file's `nose_to_axis` (10.6 in, rotary on the bare table), which is unconservative once a plate and subplate raise the A centerline.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Rotary subplate** = a new built-in accessory kind `rotary_subplate` (`Accessory::RotarySubplate`: length, width, thickness, bore spacing, first bore from -X, bores from -Y, bore diameter). Generic default figures, named generic (10 x 6 x 3/4 in, 1/2 in bores 6 in apart) - no maker's dimensions committed; the user enters theirs. Solid-slab mesh (bores drawn solid). It lands **fixed** (never in the swept radius). Its frame is the first pin bore at the underside, +X toward the second, so `PlaceOnPlate` seats it on a #819 dowel pair by its pins.\n- **Pin law:** a subplate goes only on a dowel pair whose spacing equals its bore spacing (0.05 mm); a single hole or another spacing is refused by name - at `PlaceOnPlate`, at a `SetPlate` re-seat, and at a `SetAccessory` resize of the placed subplate (which also keeps its footprint on the plate).\n- **Raised centerline** (`app::rotary_stack`): the setup's subplates and every plate under each (through the plate locations) form a stack; the tallest one is used. The swing clause judges with the **effective** `nose_to_axis` = machine figure less the stack, or the setup's **stated** figure, which wins.\n- **Refusal law:** a stack whose thickness is unknown (an imported plate under the subplate, a vanished or looped plate, a non-finite figure), a stated figure that is no length, or an effective figure at or under zero refuses the swing **by name** - never judged on the table figure. **No subplate: judged word for word as before** (pinned by the exact message).\n- **Per-setup stated figure:** `SetupDef::nose_to_axis`, command `SetSetupNoseToAxis` (finite, > 0, <= 5000 mm; no-op refused; undoable), carried by a datum transfer with the machine.\n- **Save/load:** additive setup key `nose_to_axis`; the subplate rides the existing `accessory` key. Old files load unchanged (pinned).\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/821-rotary-on-plate-stack.md`.\n\n## Commands, MCP, UI\n\n- Commands: `InsertAccessory` / `SetAccessory` (new kind), `PlaceOnPlate` (pin law), new `SetSetupNoseToAxis`.\n- MCP: `add_accessory` / `set_accessory` take `rotary_subplate`; `place_on_plate` applies the pin law; new `get_rotary_stack` (stack layers, stated figure, machine rotaries, refusal reason) and `set_setup_nose_to_axis` (number or null).\n- UI: the Fixtures page's accessory dialog lists \"Rotary subplate\" (KINDS-driven); the setup's Machine page gets a \"Rotary centerline\" section (machine figure, the stack readout or the refusal, a checkbox + field for the setup's stated figure, queued as `CommandKind::SetupNoseToAxis`). Drawn only for a machine with a work-turning rotary. No snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/rotary_subplate.rs` (new): `a_subplate_lands_fixed_and_seats_on_a_dowel_pair_by_its_pins`, `the_same_program_clears_on_the_table_and_is_refused_on_the_stack`, `a_stack_of_unknown_thickness_is_refused_by_name`, `an_effective_nose_at_or_under_zero_is_refused_by_name`, `the_setup_s_stated_nose_wins_and_is_an_undoable_command`, `no_stack_is_judged_word_for_word_as_before`, `the_subplate_and_the_stated_nose_survive_a_save_and_old_files_load_unchanged`.\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp_rotary_stack.rs` (new): `a_subplate_is_pinned_on_a_plate_and_raises_the_rotary_over_mcp`.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/setup_rotary.rs` (new, AccessKit labels): `the_stated_nose_is_one_undoable_command`, `the_machine_page_shows_the_rotary_rows_and_states_the_figure`, `a_machine_without_a_work_turning_rotary_draws_no_rotary_rows`.\n- `builtin_accessory` updated for the sixth kind (KINDS, bounds/volume of the slab, insert order).\n- Gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green on 642cd694 (app suites 365 s, index_swing_horizontal 10 fn, ui suites 44 s; 0 failed). By hand (not mapped by quick, #1021): index_swing 9/9, index_swing_horizontal 10/10, tormach_fourth_axis 12/12, rotary_fixtures 4/4, rotary_verify 9/9; ui lib `setup_rotary`, `accessory`, `fixture`, `structural` filters 51/51; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- **The hardware check on the user's own microARC subplate** (#821 \"Checked on the user's microARC subplate\") - stays with the user; hence `Refs`, not `Fixes`.\n- The camcraft-mcp skill's tool table is not updated (a process file; the new tools describe themselves in `tools/list`).\n- Posed collision judgement of the subplate itself is the existing fixed-fixture law (unchanged).\n\nChangelog: A rotary subplate (built-in accessory) is placed on a fixture plate's dowel pair by its pin bores, and the A index-swing check judges from the centerline the subplate and plate stack raise - or from the setup's stated nose_to_axis - refusing by name when the stack's thickness is unknown (#821)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nRefs #821\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
